From adc4e92280125032d536ef68065ee6524d43aca4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kimwooseok <ssassa601@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:51:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] debian: backport WPA-PSK authentication retries for known
 profiles

A previously successful WPA-PSK profile can request a new key after a
4-way-handshake failure, including when connection.auth-retries is zero.

Backport the upstream retry getter, retry-availability helper and WPA-PSK
StateChanged handling to Raspberry Pi OS Trixie network-manager 1.52.1-1+rpt4.
Apply the CONFIG-state guard and reuse the stored key while retries remain.

On a Pi 5, a 45-second test with a temporary wrong PSK and auth-retries=0
recorded eight stored-key retries and zero new-key requests. The base package
recorded zero stored-key retries and one new-key request in the same window.
The native arm64 build produced nine packages. The focused C regression
harness passed 24 cases and 580 assertions.

Upstream: a3267aaf7bfab66604b2a6e69973301bb7f9b867
Upstream: 6dc51ddf01afe790bcf48d93192a0e535987334e
Upstream: 746a5902ad85ec0611a3e6ebfd7b68b45621a40b
Upstream: 6dd07a80e535a2e76e7304c92d4db97097af98a4 (CONFIG guard)
---
 debian/changelog                              |   9 +
 ...wifi-backport-known-psk-auth-retries.patch | 221 ++++++++++++++++++
 debian/patches/series                         |   1 +
 3 files changed, 231 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 debian/patches/0001-wifi-backport-known-psk-auth-retries.patch

diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index c73a691..79efc30 100644
